<title>USA: Northrop Grumman wins JSTARS contract.</title>
<headline>Northrop Grumman wins JSTARS contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Air Force said it has awarded a $254 million contract to Northrop Grumman, Grumman Aerospace Corp. for follow-on test support for the JSTARS ground surveillance plane.</p>
<p>JSTARS (Joint Surveillance Target Attack Radar System) is a plane that identifies enemy targets on the ground in combat and relays information on them to U.S. field commanders.</p>
</text>
